{"id": "2026-07-27-news-wildfires-push-300-000-from-homes-near-bordeaux", "date": "2026-07-27", "stream": "news", "headline": "Wildfires push 300,000 from homes near Bordeaux", "summary": "Wildfires around Bordeaux forced one of France's largest-ever evacuations, with around 300,000 people moved across France and Spain and a new heatwave forecast from Tuesday.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/international/rekordbraende-wegen-trockenheit-heftige-waldbraende-in-frankreich-und-spanien-die-aktuelle-lage", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Wildfires around Bordeaux drove one of the largest evacuations in French history, with around 300,000 people now moved to safety across France and Spain and the flames roughly 15 km from the city. In southwest France the fire in the Gironde has burned more than 19,000 hectares and destroyed about 100 buildings since Wednesday, forcing some 220,000 people from their homes — 55,000 more ordered out around Bordeaux over the weekend, and 31,000 in neighbouring Landes; boats were used to evacuate holidaymakers from the Cap Ferret peninsula. Interior Minister Laurent Nuñez said the blaze turned \"extremely violent and unpredictable\" overnight, the A63 motorway to Spain is shut over about 60 km, and nearly 100,000 hectares have burned nationwide since January — a historic record. In Spain the government declared a state of emergency around Madrid and in Ávila (where about 47,000 hectares burned), with roughly 90,000 people evacuated according to the interior ministry; El País reports the Madrid, Ávila and Toledo fires have covered some 77,000 hectares in all. A new heatwave with temperatures up to 40°C is forecast from Tuesday 28 July, threatening to worsen the fight.", "why": "This is the sharp escalation of a fire emergency running across France, Spain and Italy since 23 July — the direct threat to Bordeaux, a metropolis of about 850,000, and the incoming heat push it well beyond the earlier evacuations.", "thread_id": "2026-07-23-news-wildfires-kill-three-firefighters-across-france", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-23", "event_date": "2026-07-23", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["France", "Spain", "Bordeaux", "Madrid"]}
{"id": "2026-07-27-news-iran-vows-retaliation-over-caspian-sea-strike", "date": "2026-07-27", "stream": "news", "headline": "Iran vows retaliation over Caspian Sea strike", "summary": "Iran summoned Ukraine's envoy and threatened reprisals after a Ukrainian strike killed a sailor on an Iranian Caspian Sea vessel, as a US-Iran strike pause held a second day.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/7/27/iran-warns-ukraine-of-retaliation-after-deadly-caspian-sea-strike", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Iran warned Ukraine it will retaliate for a deadly strike on an Iranian commercial vessel in the Caspian Sea, opening a new front that links the Russia–Ukraine war to the recent US–Israel conflict with Iran. Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said on Sunday 26 July that the Ukrainian attack the day before — which Iran says caused the ship to explode, killing one sailor and injuring several — \"cannot go unanswered\" and violated the UN Charter, and he accused Israel of provoking it to \"drag Europe into its war.\" Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said his forces had hit \"vessels used in military cargo shipments involving Iran, as well as a warship\" in long-range strikes, and accused Russia of feeding Iran satellite imagery of US facilities in the Gulf. Iran has summoned Ukraine's chargé d'affaires in Tehran, and a senior lawmaker said early Monday that Kyiv \"may soon come to understand that Iran does not let actions go unanswered.\" Separately, the United States and Iran held off on fresh strikes for a second straight day, and oil prices eased.", "why": "Kyiv striking an Iranian ship — over Tehran's supply of Shahed drones to Moscow since 2022 — risks pulling Iran directly into the Ukraine war just as a fragile pause in the US–Iran fighting takes hold.", "thread_id": "2026-07-27-news-iran-vows-retaliation-over-caspian-sea-strike", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-27", "event_date": "2026-07-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Iran", "Ukraine", "Caspian Sea", "Abbas Araghchi"]}
{"id": "2026-07-27-news-berlin-pride-attacker-shot-dead-by-police", "date": "2026-07-27", "stream": "news", "headline": "Berlin Pride attacker shot dead by police", "summary": "German police killed the suspect in Saturday's Berlin Pride van-ramming, treated as an Islamist terrorist attack by the interior minister; one person died and 29 were injured.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-pride-ramming-police-shoot-suspect-dead/live-78117180", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["security", "world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "German police shot dead the suspect in Saturday night's Berlin Pride van-ramming attack, which Interior Minister Alexander Dobrindt said authorities are treating as an \"Islamist terrorist attack.\" The suspect was killed in a police operation on Sunday 26 July after, police said, attacking officers with a bladed weapon; Dobrindt said there was no indication of a further threat. One person was killed and 29 injured — a higher toll than the 16 reported the day before — when the attacker drove a van into a crowd in Tiergarten Park, near the Christopher Street Day parade, one of Europe's largest LGBTQ+ celebrations. Chancellor Friedrich Merz urged marchers \"not to be intimidated,\" and the Brandenburg Gate was lit in the colours of the Pride flag for a candlelit vigil.", "why": "The \"Islamist terrorist\" classification is the interior minister's characterisation and the investigation is early, but a deadly attack on a Pride event has already prompted German calls for tighter security.", "thread_id": "2026-07-26-news-van-hits-berlin-pride-crowd-one-killed", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-26", "event_date": "2026-07-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Berlin", "Germany", "Christopher Street Day", "Alexander Dobrindt"]}
{"id": "2026-07-27-news-brazil-recalls-ambassador-after-milei-insults-lu", "date": "2026-07-27", "stream": "news", "headline": "Brazil recalls ambassador after Milei insults Lula", "summary": "Brazil recalled its ambassador to Argentina after President Milei called Lula a 'convict' and 'thief' at a Bolsonaro campaign event in São Paulo.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-recalls-ambassador-to-argentina-over-milei-s-remarks/a-78123444", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Brazil recalled its ambassador to Argentina on Sunday 26 July after President Javier Milei insulted President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva on Brazilian soil. At a São Paulo campaign event the day before for Flávio Bolsonaro — son of former far-right president Jair Bolsonaro and a likely 2026 challenger to Lula — Milei called the Brazilian leader a \"convict,\" a \"delinquent\" and a \"thief\" without naming him, and derided Supreme Court Justice Alexandre de Moraes as \"bald trash.\" Brazil's foreign ministry said there was \"no precedent for a foreign president, on national territory, to hurl insults\" at its head of state and institutions, and also summoned Argentina's ambassador.", "why": "Argentina and Brazil are each other's main regional trading partners and the core of the Mercosur bloc; a personal rupture between their presidents, tied to Argentina's libertarian right backing Brazil's far right, strains an already fraying relationship.", "thread_id": "2026-07-27-news-brazil-recalls-ambassador-after-milei-insults-lu", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-27", "event_date": "2026-07-26", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Brazil", "Argentina", "Javier Milei", "Lula da Silva"]}
{"id": "2026-07-27-news-pakistan-monsoon-floods-kill-107", "date": "2026-07-27", "stream": "news", "headline": "Pakistan monsoon floods kill 107", "summary": "Pakistan's monsoon death toll since late June reached at least 107 with 344 injured, and authorities warned of more heavy rain across Punjab this week.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/7/27/death-toll-from-pakistan-monsoon-rains-floods-tops-100", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Pakistan's monsoon death toll since late June reached at least 107, with 344 injured, and authorities warned of more heavy rain this week. The National Disaster Management Authority said Khyber Pakhtunkhwa has recorded the most deaths (55), followed by Punjab (36), and that more than half were caused by house or roof collapses. In Punjab, an irrigation official described \"a vast area of around 400 sq km\" now under water across the Lahore and Gujranwala divisions, calling it \"an inland sea\"; Lahore has set up at least 17 flood-relief camps.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-07-27-news-pakistan-monsoon-floods-kill-107", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-27", "event_date": "2026-07-26", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Pakistan", "Punjab", "Khyber Pakhtunkhwa"]}
{"id": "2026-07-27-news-swiss-crews-join-french-wildfire-fight", "date": "2026-07-27", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss crews join French wildfire fight", "summary": "Thirty-four Romand firefighters deployed to the Gironde and Switzerland's army will send two Super Puma helicopters to fight the French wildfires.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/pendant-que-des-pompiers-romands-luttent-contre-les-incendies-en-france-d-autres-se-preparent-au-pire-en-suisse", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Thirty-four firefighters from French-speaking Switzerland — mostly Geneva, with crews from Vaud and Neuchâtel — arrived in the Gironde late on Saturday 25 July and worked through the night west of Cestas, about 10 km from Bordeaux's ring road, saving much of a solar-panel farm before the wind turned; further rotations are planned through 1 August. Separately, after France requested aircraft, the Swiss defence department (DDPS) decided to deploy two Super Puma helicopters to the Var department, expected to leave on Tuesday 28 July alongside a small humanitarian-aid rapid-response team.", "why": "It is a concrete cross-border civil-protection commitment, and — with Switzerland's own forests parched — a marker of how the same drought conditions now stretch Alpine-region emergency services.", "thread_id": "2026-07-27-news-swiss-crews-join-french-wildfire-fight", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-27", "event_date": "2026-07-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland", "France", "Gironde", "DDPS"]}
{"id": "2026-07-27-news-swiss-customs-office-cuts-management-posts", "date": "2026-07-27", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss customs office cuts management posts", "summary": "Switzerland's federal customs office (OFDF) announced a restructuring cutting about 25 management posts and reverting to a pre-2023 regional structure.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/l-office-federal-des-douanes-prevoit-une-restructuration-et-la-suppression-de-25-postes-de-cadre", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Director Pascal Lüthi, in post since January 2024, told staff the agency's 23 \"local levels\" — created under former director Christian Bock, whose contract was terminated in May 2023 — will become 16 \"customs posts,\" and its six regions (including \"Douane Ouest,\" covering Geneva, Vaud and Valais) will revert to four from 1 August 2026, with new directorates in place from 1 January 2027 and a transition lasting until end-2031. Current managers must reapply for their jobs, which some staff fear will be used to remove inconvenient cadres; the office says it aims to find an internal solution for everyone affected. Reporting is drawn from CH Media titles (Aargauer Zeitung, Luzerner Zeitung, St. Galler Tagblatt).", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-07-27-news-swiss-customs-office-cuts-management-posts", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-27", "event_date": "2026-07-27", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["OFDF", "Switzerland", "Pascal Lüthi"]}
